      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1912, workers on a Western Maryland Railway cut uncovered a cave on Wills Mountain near Corriganville, later named the Cumberland Bone Cave.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corriganville%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Excavations revealed 41 mammal genera, including 16 percent extinct, with skulls dating back 200,000 years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corriganville%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Cumberland Bone Cave ranks among the finest Pleistocene faunas discovered east of the Mississippi.",
